  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The distance from the point (-1,2) of the line which passes through (2,-3)\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n=\\sqrt{(2+1)^{2}+(-3-2)^{2}} \\\\\r\n=\\sqrt{9+25}=\\sqrt{34}     < 8\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$\r\nGiven that, the distance between the point (-1,2) and the line is 8 But the maximum distance of the line passing through (2,-3) from (-1,2) is $\\sqrt{34}$. So, there is no such line possible.",
